{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Fix committed as 594f74b109c (not pushed — operator will land).\n\nVERIFICATION OF THE WINDOW FIGURES (AC3): queried the provider live Models API,\n`client.models.retrieve(<id>).max_input_tokens`:\n  claude-haiku-4-5   -> 200,000    (declared 200_000    — correct)\n  claude-sonnet-4-6  -> 1,000,000  (declared 1_000_000  — correct)\n  claude-opus-4-8    -> 1,000,000  (declared 1_000_000  — correct)\nBoth figures are RIGHT. Sonnet 4.6 and Opus 4.8 genuinely share a 1M window, so\noption 3 (correct the numbers) is ruled out by measurement, and option 1 (drop the\nopus rung) would delete a truthful table entry. The defect is in CONSUMPTION.\n\nFIX: new `sizing.escalation_rungs()` = `models_at_or_above()` minus every rung that\nis not a strict capacity increase. Consumed by BOTH context-limit retry loops\n(`pass1_with_ladder`, `prerequisites.run_focused_finder`). `models_at_or_above`,\n`MODEL_LADDER` and `largest_window_tokens` are all unchanged, so task 7761s\nprovider-stickiness suite and P8s size budget are untouched — the change is additive.\n\nMUTATION EVIDENCE (both directions):\n * Mutant A (filter neutered, escalation_rungs returns the unfiltered ladder):\n   5 tests FAIL, including the strictly-increasing guard and both behavioural\n   tests, which show the real defect — recorded model sequence contains\n   claude-opus-4-8.\n * Mutant C (opus rung window lowered to 900_000, i.e. a decreasing table):\n   the non-decreasing structural guard FAILS.\n * Unmutated: 149 passed across test_plan_review.py, test_model_class_ladder.py\n   and test_pass1_finder_model.py.\n\nGATES BY EXIT CODE: make lint = 0, make typecheck = 0 (mypy, 414 files).\nFull default selection run separately on a clean committed tree.\n\nNOTE ON TEST DESIGN: asserting `window == 1_000_000` cannot discriminate sonnet\nfrom opus (it holds for both), so every assertion is on rung IDENTITY or on the\nobserved per-attempt model sequence, never on a bare window number."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785714617740601001,"uuid":"41ff56ec-adf8-4b29-9dd3-10f226e313cc"}